  "quote_construct": "T-N, corresponding to TAF15 (exons 1-6)-NR4A3 (intron 2-exon 8) and T-N*, corresponding to the commonest TAF15 (exons 1-6)-NR4A3 (exons 3-8) fusion. Both T-N and T-N* encode the whole coding sequence of NR4A3 (exons 3-8); T-N retains a short cryptic exon located in NR4A3 intron 2 (ENST00000395097.6 isoform), thus encoding 25 additional amino acids prior to the NR4A3 ATG.",
  "quote_prevalence": "we sought to compare the biological behavior of the two major TAF15-NR4A3 isoforms detected in human tumors. Cells were engineered with the T-N* fusion variant (TAF15 exon 6-NR4A3 exon 3) and with the less common T-N variant (TAF15 exon 6-NR4A3 intron 2).",
